================================================
  PenMount Xorg Driver for Debian 10 / 11 / 12
================================================

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Supported Versions
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Distribution   : Debian 10 / 11 / 12
X.Org X Server : 1.20 / 1.21
XInput         : 24.1 / 24.4
RandR          : 1.5
GTK+           : 2.24.32 / 3.24.5
Driver         : 4.7.7.R24
Architecture   : i686 / x86_64 / armhf / aarch64

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PenMount Support
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  - PenMount 5000 series (USB, low speed)
  - PemMount 6000 series (USB, full speed)
  - PemMount P2   series (USB, full speed)
  - PemMount K1   series (USB, full speed)
  - PemMount 9000 series (Serial, 19200/9600 bps)
  - PemMount 6000 series (Serial, 19200/9600 bps)
  - PemMount P2   series (Serial, 38400 bps)

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
File Description
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  gCal             - PenMount calibration utility (without UI)
                     e.g. gCal <0|4|9|16|25> <config_file>
                     e.g. gCal 4
                          (config file is saved in /etc/penmount.dat)
                     e.g. gCal 4 /tmp/penmount.dat
                          (config file is assigned in /tmp/penmount.dat)
  gDraw            - PenMount drawing test
                     e.g. gDraw
                          gDraw cross
                          gDraw point
                          gDraw -h, see the details
  install.sh       - Install script
  gPen             - PenMount utility in GNOME tray
                     Use penmount to perform calibration and another settings.
  pm-gcalib        - (GTK3) Supports multiple device calibration and monitor mapping.
  pm-wcalib        - (GTK3) Supports calibration in Wayland, requires system restart.
  penmount*.png    - An icon files.
  penmount.dat     - Default calibration data file
                     It will be created after calibration.
  penmount.desktop - GNOME menu item entry
  penmount_drv.so  - PenMount XInput Module
  penmount.png     - An icon for GNOME menu item
  pm-setup         - PenMount setup utility. It can configure the PenMount
                     driver and X configuration file (/etc/X11/xorg.conf)
  penmount.ini     - Default settings for PenMount XInput Module

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Quick Install
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1) Open terminal

     [Activities] -> [Show Applications] -> All -> Terminal

  2) Change directory to where the device driver is extracted to

     $ cd pmlinux-Debian9

  3) Change the settings in PenMount.ini or just use the default configurations.

  4) Run install script with root permission
     $ sudo ./install.sh

  5) Restart X window system to apply changes

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Calibration
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  1) Start the PenMount Utility.

     In [Activities] -> [Show Applications] -> All -> PenMount Utility

     The PenMount utility will be launched.

  2) Select calibrate type and press the 'Calibrate' button.

  3) Follow the instuctions on screen and finish calibration.

  * gCal is the calibration utility can be run directly in terminal.
    gCal [4|9|16|25] - advanced calibration (4 points, 9 points...)

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Application Notes
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
(1) Currently the PenMount device driver does not support wayland yet.
(2) For Using pinch gesture in google chrome, please switch the operation mode to "touch" mode using the PenMount Utility.
